# Security Baseline

## Authentication & Authorization
- MUST verify JWT via `authJwt.verifyToken` on every protected REST route
- MUST check group permissions via `verifyGroups()` before admin or write operations
- MUST enforce `isSocketWriteAuthorized()` / `isSocketAdminAuthorized()` on Socket.io handlers
- MUST apply `express-rate-limit` on auth endpoints (see `server/api/index.js`)
- NEVER bypass auth when `settings.secureEnabled` is true

## Secrets Handling
- MUST read secrets from `settings.secretCode` / runtime config, not hardcoded strings
- NEVER commit `.env`, API keys, JWT secrets, or `server/_appdata/` databases
- NEVER log tokens, passwords, or `secretCode` values
- Test secrets MUST be isolated constants in test files only

## Input Validation
- MUST validate and normalize file paths (see `server/api/path-helper.js` patterns)
- MUST reject path traversal (`..`, absolute paths outside allowed dirs)
- MUST cap request body size via `apiMaxLength` setting (default `100mb`)
- MUST sanitize user-supplied script content before `runtime/scripts` execution
- NEVER pass unsanitized user input to `eval()`, `Function()`, or shell commands

## Dependency Hygiene
- MUST NOT add dependencies without user approval and security review
- MUST run `npm audit` in affected package before merging dependency changes
- MUST use `server/package.json` `overrides` for known vulnerable transitive deps
- NEVER install packages from unverified git URLs or non-npm registries

## Industrial / SCADA Safety
- MUST validate device write commands against tag permissions before dispatch
- MUST NOT expose internal device connection strings in API responses
- Alarm acknowledge and script execution MUST require authenticated, authorized users
